@page "/docs/mcp"
@layout Layout.DocsLayout

<PageTitle>MCP server · blux-ui</PageTitle>
<div class="pg-prose">
    <p class="pg-eyebrow">AI</p>
    <h1>MCP server</h1>
    <p class="pg-lead">Give your AI coding agent the real API of every component, so it stops guessing parameter names.</p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>
        The Model Context Protocol server answers from the same documentation as this site: the catalog, the parameters, events and slots read
        from the library, the theme slots, the source of every example and the guides. It is generated at build time, so it cannot drift from the code.
    </p>
    <p>Tools, all read-only:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>search-components</code>: find components by name, family, alternate name (dialog finds Modal) or intent. Without a query it lists them all.</li>
        <li><code>get-component</code>: one component as Markdown, by section: <code>usage</code>, <code>examples</code>, <code>api</code>, <code>theme</code>.</li>
        <li><code>get-component-metadata</code>: parameters, events, slots and <code>Ui</code> slots as JSON, compact by default, <code>full</code> for descriptions and allowed values.</li>
        <li><code>list-examples</code> and <code>get-example</code>: the live examples of this site and their Razor source.</li>
        <li><code>search-documentation</code> and <code>get-documentation-page</code>: full-text search and pages of the guides and components.</li>
        <li><code>search-icons</code>: the built-in icon names.</li>
        <li><code>get-installation-guide</code>: setup for a render mode (<code>auto</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>wasm</code>, <code>ssr</code>) and a CSS mode (<code>precompiled</code>, <code>tailwind</code>).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Prompts: <code>find-component-for-usecase</code> and <code>implement-component-with-props</code>. Resources:
        <code>resource://blux-ui/components</code>, <code>resource://blux-ui/examples</code> and <code>resource://blux-ui/documentation-pages</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Local server, over stdio</h2>
    <p>The <code>Blux.UI.Mcp</code> dotnet tool runs offline and carries the documentation of the Blux UI version it was built with. It needs the .NET 10 runtime.</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="dotnet tool install --global Blux.UI.Mcp --prerelease" />
    <p>Register it with Claude Code:</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="claude mcp add --transport stdio blux-ui -- blux-ui-mcp" />
    <p>Add <code>--scope project</code> to share it through the <code>.mcp.json</code> of the repository. Everything after <code>--</code> is the command, so options go there:</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="claude mcp add --transport stdio blux-ui -- blux-ui-mcp --tools search-components,get-component,get-component-metadata" />

    <h2>Remote server, over HTTP</h2>
    <p>This site serves the same server at <code>/mcp</code> (Streamable HTTP, stateless). Replace the address with the host of the site:</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="claude mcp add --transport http blux-ui https://your-docs-host/mcp" />
    <p>To expose only some tools, send their names in the <code>X-MCP-Tools</code> header:</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@HttpHeader" />

    <h2>Cursor</h2>
    <p>In <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> (or <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>):</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="mcp.json" Code="@Cursor" />

    <h2>VS Code</h2>
    <p>In <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="mcp.json" Code="@VsCode" />

    <h2>Windsurf</h2>
    <p>In <code>~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json</code>:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="mcp_config.json" Code="@Windsurf" />

    <h2>Options of the local tool</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><code>--tools a,b</code> exposes only those tools, like the <code>X-MCP-Tools</code> header.</li>
        <li><code>--site-url https://...</code> puts the address of the docs site in front of page paths in answers.</li>
        <li><code>--list-tools</code> and <code>--version</code> print and exit.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    private const string HttpHeader = """
        claude mcp add --transport http blux-ui https://your-docs-host/mcp --header "X-MCP-Tools: search-components,get-component"
        """;

    private const string Cursor = """
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "blux-ui": { "command": "blux-ui-mcp" }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string VsCode = """
        {
          "servers": {
            "blux-ui": { "type": "stdio", "command": "blux-ui-mcp" },
            "blux-ui-remote": { "type": "http", "url": "https://your-docs-host/mcp" }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string Windsurf = """
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "blux-ui": { "command": "blux-ui-mcp" }
          }
        }
        """;
}
